Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-20-2000||05:46 PM||||I still can't get the left distributor screw to hold it down. I have tried retapping, but being the idiot I am, I went in at a sort of angle. How bad would it be if I drilled the hole bigger (In both the cap and the distributor) and then just put a bolt and nut through? Think it would be that bad?||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||11-20-2000||06:18 PM||||It's always the <B>left screw</B>, isn't it? You're not alone.  Screwed up screw? Take a look about 1/3 of the way down, in this "thread"      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">:   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005374.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005374.html</A> <P>Hope you're helped     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-----------------------------------<BR>Ooops! That <B>was</B> you before, wasn't it?  Well, the oddball  (longer) screw + nut on underside method still works.  And, if you used the epoxy repair, but  "angle-tapped" it, you can still re-epoxy, re-drill and retap until you get it right    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !  Takes patience and care, that's all    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||10
